Origin: applejack
Date: 2026-11-08
Reason: NtQueryDirectoryObject's unix side, built by clang for macOS, tests
 its BOOLEAN `restart` argument with `testl %r8d, %r8d`: clang assumes the
 caller zero-extended it. A PE caller writes only the low byte (kernelbase's
 GetLogicalDrives stores `movb $0x0, 0x20(%rsp)`), so stale stack bytes above
 it read as "restart", every call returns the first entry of \DosDevices with
 context 1, and GetLogicalDrives never returns. The Steam client calls it from
 WMI (`SELECT * FROM Win32_DiskPartition`) on its MachineIDInfoThread, and
 its CM connect (CCMInterface EConnect) waits for that thread, logging
 `EConnect called - scheduling connection for 50ms from now` ten times a
 second and never connecting. Measured 2026-11-08 with Tailscale and NetBird
 up: winedbg backtraces of MachineIDInfoThread in GetLogicalDrives
 (fill_diskpartition) across 25 s; a probe looping NtQueryDirectoryObject on
 \DosDevices got the same entry 3,000 times (context 1) and never returned
 from GetLogicalDrives; with the patch it lists 47 entries in under 2 ms, and
 the client logs `YieldingConnect` and `ConnectionCompleted` instead of the
 storm (two runs, 0 `EConnect called` lines), against 304 to 711 lines in
 each 30 to 60 s window of five runs with the stock ntdll.so on the same host
 the same afternoon. See "The CM connect loop" in docs/steam-runtime.md.
 The same 32-bit read of a register-passed BOOLEAN is left unpatched in
 NtDelayExecution and NtContinue (alertable), NtDuplicateToken
 (effective_only), and NtQueryDefaultLocale and NtSetDefaultLocale (user);
 NtAdjustPrivilegesToken stores its BOOLEAN `disable` as 32 bits into the
 server request's int `disable_all`, which wineserver tests whole. None has
 been seen to fail. build/wine/patches/README.md lists them and how to
 check a new build.
Drop-when: upstream wine's dlls/ntdll/unix/sync.c NtQueryDirectoryObject
 no longer reads its BOOLEAN arguments as wider than a byte, the unix side
 stops being built with clang, or the x86_64 syscall dispatcher
 zero-extends sub-int arguments before calling the unix side; check each
 Wine bump.

--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/sync.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/sync.c
@@ -1930,9 +1930,18 @@
                                         ULONG *context, ULONG *ret_size )
 {
     unsigned int status, i, count, total_len, pos, used_size, used_count, strpool_head;
-    ULONG index = restart ? 0 : *context;
+    ULONG index;
     struct directory_entry *entries;
 
+    /* A PE caller sets only the low byte of a BOOLEAN argument, in a register
+     * or a stack slot, while clang assumes it arrives zero-extended and tests
+     * 32 bits; a stale byte above it reads as "restart" and a single-entry
+     * enumeration such as GetLogicalDrives gets the first entry forever.
+     * Reloading each through memory keeps the low byte alone. */
+    single_entry = *(volatile BOOLEAN *)&single_entry;
+    restart = *(volatile BOOLEAN *)&restart;
+    index = restart ? 0 : *context;
+
     if (!(entries = malloc( size ))) return STATUS_NO_MEMORY;
 
     SERVER_START_REQ( get_directory_entries )
